tps://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whitej031788/jamie-nx/commits/f339a1ab4052a0eb020d85a1ef974b39cebf0c68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-05-08T21:29:10Z","email":"xiongemi@gmail.com","name":"Emily Xiong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-05-08T21:29:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gradle): fix gradle tests (#30879)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\ncurrently, because it requires to sign locally, so i thought run command\nlike\n`:project-graph:publishToMavenLocal -x\n:project-graph:signNxProjectGraphPluginPluginMarkerMavenPublication -x\n:project-graph:signPluginMavenPublication -x\n:project-graph:publishNxProjectGraphPluginPluginMarkerMavenPublicationToMavenLocal\n-x :project-graph:publishPluginMavenPublicationToMavenLocal` would\npublish the plugin locally, but it actually does not. it does not throw\nan error, but does not do anything at all.\nso for e2e tests, it is actually pulling the latest published gradle\nplugin from maven rather than test local code, hence the e2e errors.\n\nalso, currently project graph build for java version 21, we change it to\njava 17 to be used by ocean repo.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\nchange the command to `./gradlew :project-graph:publishToMavenLocal\n-PskipSign=true` and not apply signing when skip sign is true, so this\nshould be able to publish plugin to local repository.\n\nwork with java 17\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes #","tree":{"sha":"cfb354c2c60b447234c0fa7ef4ee303bbbef9295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whitej031788/jamie-nx/git/trees/cfb354c2c60b447234c0fa7ef4ee303bbbef9295"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whitej031788/jamie-nx/git/commits/f339a1ab4052a0eb020d85a1ef974b39cebf0c68","verification":{"payload":"tree cfb354c2c60b447234c0fa7ef4ee303bbbef9295\nparent 468ec023c551b2414417b464efc575b6e601be44\nauthor Emily Xiong <xiongemi@gmail.com> 1746739750 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1746739750 -0400\n\nfix(gradle): fix gradle tests (#30879)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\ncurrently, because it requires to sign locally, so i thought run command\nlike\n`:project-graph:publishToMavenLocal -x\n:project-graph:signNxProjectGraphPluginPluginMarkerMavenPublication -x\n:project-graph:signPluginMavenPublication -x\n:project-graph:publishNxProjectGraphPluginPluginMarkerMavenPublicationToMavenLocal\n-x :project-graph:publishPluginMavenPublicationToMavenLocal` would\npublish the plugin locally, but it actually does not. it does not throw\nan error, but does not do anything at all.\nso for e2e tests, it is actually pulling the latest published gradle\nplugin from maven rather than test local code, hence the e2e errors.\n\nalso, currently project graph build for java version 21, we change it to\njava 17 to be used by ocean repo.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\nchange the command to `./gradlew :project-graph:publishToMavenLocal\n-PskipSign=true` and not apply signing when skip sign is true, so this\nshould be able to publish plugin to local repository.\n\nwork with java 17\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes #","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoHSImCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhIEQAHR/E3tZlc3s1HWHQyzljaQe\nh/m2DzmzdGIwErMaGofAL06eAmPBOXe0W1IsqgTFTErnygIplFJUAbA0bt5mrlj9\n9Xwyt4pepDD0K5h8O+PbslM/Uoa4JVB+N8jcqiBCk8q+TNuW4nxa727/JodMiz41\nLWptjNlFlUGcGwxL2nX6u47tSxxVNxTz387DbZjxKqKx2Ym95k99MFkebpDob38D\nfNfpEzRHohl3s1GVPm8ywTe6ZkbO9Tph4Ttr8d4y+6zIb5TwvWA0tlOc458/b4UA\nRF6pyOFk0Jf0hA8LTkH+n2JpWvBcIJknPVyRMCPxljLaG89YKV18nayT1S2QNYl2\nAoC3nLjCK3J2gHHAJ1URvurPzMvp4G3m2PRpSUsGnjCpJ0DXesyulDm7DolXzQTt\nIxeaLCqP4ZxP1iIMCoC71rOqA5wGyYxfDaDsJu7D2mWGlScMk0ZYZwfHidVE13si\nwjwN+hsXih7XhSnAgryi3IPczTbGSQPgzeqz3F+fASzTdKAuWw+Ka0yQy4X2WWZJ\ncmjzutVe23nN6DfqI2TtnKTGq5fRlDLaJfziMq7cQDiUWrsgkd+POFoZmNsET6aR\nHaS0kj1XtGKFXOMTJ7Z+IMVPcq1aawLrRW9HvTVQrqR2/gpD3olPFNAJwsVJv0pP\nef422+YMYI/hhlDxrXNE\n=PoYo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-05-16T19:40:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.git