,"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiongemi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whitej031788/jamie-nx/commits/468ec023c551b2414417b464efc575b6e601be44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-05-08T21:26:16Z","email":"xiongemi@gmail.com","name":"Emily Xiong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-05-08T21:26:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gradle): specify idle timeout for gradle batch runner (#31009)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\nthere is no idle timeout set for gradle, by default is 3 hours.\nwhen running gradle in DTE, it seems to run into memory issue. Even\nthrough using tooling api, the connection is closed when batch is done,\nbut i think the gradle daemon is still active in the background. when\nrunning the next batch, it is going to start a new gradle daemon and i\ngot an error like\n```\nStarting a Gradle Daemon, 2 busy and 200 stopped Daemons could not be reused, use --status for details\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\nadd idle timeout for 10s.\nthis inline command will make gradle daemon to stop itself after 10s.\n\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes #","tree":{"sha":"2eaa899c122093decb4e8398748f806916a8ff8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whitej031788/jamie-nx/git/trees/2eaa899c122093decb4e8398748f806916a8ff8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whitej031788/jamie-nx/git/commits/468ec023c551b2414417b464efc575b6e601be44","verification":{"payload":"tree 2eaa899c122093decb4e8398748f806916a8ff8b\nparent aea60e1a5ee0ab701b6c9b029d78a39a86b4a858\nauthor Emily Xiong <xiongemi@gmail.com> 1746739576 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1746739576 -0400\n\nfix(gradle): specify idle timeout for gradle batch runner (#31009)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\nthere is no idle timeout set for gradle, by default is 3 hours.\nwhen running gradle in DTE, it seems to run into memory issue. Even\nthrough using tooling api, the connection is closed when batch is done,\nbut i think the gradle daemon is still active in the background. when\nrunning the next batch, it is going to start a new gradle daemon and i\ngot an error like\n```\nStarting a Gradle Daemon, 2 busy and 200 stopped Daemons could not be reused, use --status for details\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\nadd idle timeout for 10s.\nthis inline command will make gradle daemon to stop itself after 10s.\n\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes #","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoHSF4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe1AQACCF/HKXVhyhGyOFKjEYNm9L\nmUChaWo1S1VsAJyG3w9dfNWLgls1iM1JiJOSDlXMZkX7kHeC19VjYPsLBsO9Qhbb\nx46nQLqKWylJw7HTG87Hp9jo+wYj8zKOGX0lPOwIdNJcK5Frj1H5VorbtYnZMZKm\nc0fms02qw6FZmNrjp8sOzhwMHucyWt7wrSpaaK1ToOXycNlGno0MRBPksPE3MYka\nc349eFlLL9SpGg49U7ZTYLZ6s0R82U1alc8TnJgoxC9K64hobg8umxk2JOd0p8G+\n7Gu1IiZgswb/tuAiJ7u57RzShZbHoe0eUfiR/YtZaqDr+/u0qZfKOgvaIbj+lzGb\ng1TsxWBaFgGGgEKb599/4k0gJTz9fvxB4pqa8WsD2OlucoagZOzID+x31cM2sWCC\nyliq2vZL/LNflVof447zfXz7e+HbIkjQ8ZiGz8+Nyj+rVFLzj6vkUABA5IHCEKUG\n3on0eraxfKIMNBaMf1/zUcmNRYDRrQRT3VizIHh6saW9GN3N2MdXYI1pc4C/JciY\nxXhNXFBrLyiYqYnOwRvpJkbwnke76FOmb3TN3oGanWWl3mPTDh26+DJwloWWKTqW\nlSJP1OUK+WwiznQ/MQfTBt4y9pU5HILssdwSS5c5EBJ8/VsQodwhLJMe3ZyCsXiL\n+goNaCzH3KOInY9dxSEN\n=xRb6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-05-16T19:40:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/r